Heres some things that will be in future REGISTERED versions. 

68010/20/30 Versions. For maximum speed, compatibilty.

Virus checking/removing on ".exe" files. (integrating
it to work with Virus Checker V6.00 by John Veldthuis.)

Expanding the config file so that any  archivers can 
be fairly easily added by you. 

Archiving of text files which were uploaded. Saving you
atleast 30% of disk space for each text file.

Different 'advertising' texts for different ud sections.

Checking of Adopted files that the sysop has "uploaded". (maybe,
this one might be a hard one.)

When a file fails upload checking, mark it unvalidated, and 
holding credits until the file is validated by a sysop/subop.

Conversion of DMS "simple" compression modes to "deep".
Done quietly in the background. Again saving you much disk space.

Removal of other dms texts, warp texts, etc. Thus saving you
MUCH disk space. Figure a dms text added by other bbs's
using HSCHK, could be as much as 20k, or more added per file. Think
about 20k times 10 files is 200k of wasted disk space. Disk
space wasted advertising other bbs's.

Correcting of bbs data files, if a dms text, etc is added,
the bbs data files will show the file being smaller
than it actually is. I plan on writing a routine
to update bbs data files to reflect any changes to a
file. Ie you wont have to ADOPT converted files.



